\mt1 Haggay
\is1 Introduction
\ip This document contains a number of messages from Yahweh that the prophet Haggay passed on to the people in Yerushalem (Jerusalem). These events happened around 520 before Yeshua/Jesus (B.C.), after many of God's people had gone back to Yerushalem after being taken into captivity in Bavel. However, even though they'd been back for a considerable time, they hadn't worked on rebuilding the temple. Therefore, these messages from Yahweh encourage the people to change their priorities and obey God and rebuild the temple. God then promised to prosper the people and bless their living situation.
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 God's command to rebuild the temple \ior 1:1-15\ior*
\io1 Stories of comfort and hope \ior 2:1-23\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
